---
const repo = 'https://github.com/mhermon/sec-fid';
---

<section class="section-rule" id="use">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="split-copy">
      <h2>Run the benchmark</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        The SecFid repository includes the benchmark data and evaluation code.
        Generate responses from any model or defense, then score them locally.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row use-actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href={repo}>Repository</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal">
<pre class="shell"><code><span class="c"># clone the benchmark</span>
<span class="g">$</span> git clone https://github.com/mhermon/sec-fid.git

<span class="c"># generate one response for each example, then score them</span>
<span class="g">$</span> python sec-fid/minimal/evaluate.py \
    --dataset sec-fid/minimal/data/secfid.jsonl \
    --responses responses.jsonl \
    --summary summary.json
<span class="c"># reports security, fidelity, safe processing, and labels</span></code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .use-actions { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
</style>
